@node Introduction
@chapter Introduction

@code{dired-image-thumbnail} is an Emacs package that extends
@code{image-dired} with an enhanced workflow inspired by
@code{dired-video-thumbnail}.  It adds powerful sorting, filtering,
subdirectory management, and flexible display options to the standard
@code{image-dired} thumbnail viewer.

@node Features
@chapter Features

@itemize @bullet
@item
@strong{Sorting} --- Sort thumbnails by name, date, size, or image dimensions
@item
@strong{Filtering} --- Filter by name regexp, file size range, or dimension range
@item
@strong{Subdirectory support} --- Works seamlessly with Dired's inserted subdirectories
@item
@strong{Subdirectory helpers} --- Commands to quickly insert/remove subdirectories
@item
@strong{Wrap display mode} --- Thumbnails flow naturally and wrap to window width
@item
@strong{Enhanced header line} --- Shows current image info, directory location, dimensions, sort/filter status, and quality level
@item
@strong{Configurable window layout} --- Six layout presets (left-right, right-left, top-bottom, bottom-top, thumb-only, manual)
@item
@strong{Display quality levels} --- Five quality tiers (full/high/fast/faster/draft) for speed vs fidelity trade-off
@item
@strong{External-tool preview generation} --- Uses @code{djpeg}/@code{cjpeg} or @code{magick} for genuinely faster image previews
@item
@strong{Image file validation} --- Magic-byte header checks and minimum file size to exclude corrupt files
@item
@strong{Open in external editor} --- Press @kbd{W} to open an image in GIMP, Krita, or your system default
@item
@strong{Auto-display navigation} --- Navigate with @kbd{n}/@kbd{p} to automatically show full-size images
@item
@strong{Enhanced deletion} --- Delete and advance with @kbd{C-d} in both thumbnail and image buffers
@item
@strong{Full integration} --- Works seamlessly with existing @code{image-dired} functionality
@item
@strong{Transient menus} --- Optional @code{transient.el} integration for discoverability
@end itemize

@node Requirements
@chapter Requirements

@itemize @bullet
@item
Emacs 28.1 or later
@item
@code{image-dired} (built-in)
@item
@code{transient} (optional, for transient menu support)
@end itemize

