@node Quick Start
@section Quick Start

The simplest way to use @code{dired-image-thumbnail} is from a Dired buffer:

@enumerate
@item
Navigate to a directory containing images
@item
Press @kbd{C-t d} (or @kbd{C-t m}) to view thumbnails
@item
Thumbnails appear on the left, full-size image on the right
@item
Navigate with @kbd{n}/@kbd{p} to automatically view each image
@item
Use the enhanced keybindings for sorting, filtering, etc.
@end enumerate

@node Working with Subdirectories
@section Working with Subdirectories

@code{dired-image-thumbnail} works with Dired's subdirectory insertion
feature.  You have several options:

@subheading Manual insertion

Use Dired's built-in @kbd{i} (@code{dired-maybe-insert-subdir}) on any
subdirectory to make its contents visible, then run
@code{dired-image-thumbnail}.

@subheading Helper commands

@itemize @bullet
@item
@kbd{C-t s} (@code{dired-image-thumbnail-insert-image-subdirs}) --- Insert only subdirectories containing images (recommended)
@item
@kbd{C-t z} (@code{dired-image-thumbnail-insert-subdir-recursive}) --- Insert all subdirectories
@item
@kbd{C-t k} (@code{dired-image-thumbnail-kill-all-subdirs}) --- Remove all inserted subdirectories
@end itemize

@node From Standard image-dired
@section From Standard image-dired

You can also use the standard @code{image-dired} commands (@kbd{C-t d},
@kbd{C-t a}, etc.) --- @code{dired-image-thumbnail} automatically enhances
the thumbnail buffer with new keybindings.

@node Enhanced Workflow
@chapter Enhanced Workflow

@code{dired-image-thumbnail} provides an enhanced grid-view workflow that
improves upon standard @code{image-dired}.

@menu
* Automatic Split-Screen Layout:: Configurable window arrangements
* Auto-Display Navigation::       Hands-free image browsing
* Quick Deletion Workflow::       Fast photo culling
@end menu

@node Automatic Split-Screen Layout
@section Automatic Split-Screen Layout

When you launch @code{dired-image-thumbnail} (or use standard
@code{image-dired} with this package loaded):

@example
+------------------+------------------------+
|  Thumbnails      |  Full-size Image       |
|  (Left 40%)      |  (Right 60%)           |
|                  |                        |
|  [img1] <--      |  +------------------+  |
|  [img2]          |  |                  |  |
|  [img3]          |  |   Current Image  |  |
|  [img4]          |  |                  |  |
|  [img5]          |  +------------------+  |
|                  |                        |
+------------------+------------------------+
@end example

The layout is controlled by @code{dired-image-thumbnail-window-layout}
(default @code{left-right}) and @code{dired-image-thumbnail-window-ratio}
(default @code{0.4}).

@node Auto-Display Navigation
@section Auto-Display Navigation

With @code{dired-image-thumbnail-auto-display-on-navigate} enabled (default):

@itemize @bullet
@item
Press @kbd{n} or @kbd{p} to navigate thumbnails
@item
The full-size image automatically updates on the right
@item
No need to press @key{RET} or @kbd{C-@key{RET}} for each image
@item
Smooth, fluid browsing experience
@end itemize

@node Quick Deletion Workflow
@section Quick Deletion Workflow

Press @kbd{C-d} in either the thumbnail or image display buffer to:

@enumerate
@item
Get a confirmation prompt (unless @code{dired-image-thumbnail-auto-accept} is enabled)
@item
Delete the current image file
@item
Automatically advance to the next image
@item
Continue browsing seamlessly
@end enumerate

This makes culling large photo collections much faster than the standard workflow.

@node Keybindings
@chapter Keybindings

@menu
* Dired Buffer Keys::           Keys available in Dired
* Thumbnail Buffer Keys::       Keys in the thumbnail buffer
