@node Dired Buffer Keys
@section In Dired Buffer

@table @kbd
@item C-t d
Launch standard image-dired enhanced (@code{image-dired} + @code{dired-image-thumbnail-refresh})
@item C-t m
Launch enhanced thumbnail viewer (@code{dired-image-thumbnail})
@item C-t s
Insert subdirs with images (@code{dired-image-thumbnail-insert-image-subdirs})
@item C-t z
Insert all subdirs recursively (@code{dired-image-thumbnail-insert-subdir-recursive})
@item C-t k
Remove all inserted subdirs (@code{dired-image-thumbnail-kill-all-subdirs})
@end table

@node Thumbnail Buffer Keys
@section In Thumbnail Buffer

@subheading Navigation

@table @kbd
@item n
@itemx @key{RIGHT}
Next image (auto-display when enabled)
@item p
@itemx @key{LEFT}
Previous image (auto-display when enabled)
@item +
Increase thumbnail size
@item -
Decrease thumbnail size
@end table

When @code{dired-image-thumbnail-auto-display-on-navigate} is enabled (default),
pressing @kbd{n} or @kbd{p} automatically displays the full-size image.

@subheading Sorting

@table @kbd
@item s b
Sort by Dired buffer order
@item s n
Sort by filename
@item s d
Sort by modification date
@item s s
Sort by file size
@item s D
Sort by image dimensions (area)
@item s r
Reverse sort order
@item S
Interactive sort selection (transient)
@end table

@subheading Filtering

@table @kbd
@item / n
Filter by name regexp
@item / s
Filter by file size range
@item / d
Filter by dimension range
@item / /
@itemx / c
Clear all filters
@item \
Interactive filter menu (transient)
@end table

@subheading Display

@table @kbd
@item w
Toggle wrap display mode
@item r
@itemx g
Refresh the display
@item G
Clear cache and refresh (hard refresh)
@item +
Increase thumbnail size
@item -
Decrease thumbnail size
@item Q
Cycle display quality (full, high, fast, faster, draft)
@end table

@subheading Marking

@table @kbd
@item m
Mark image (uses image-dired's native marking with border)
@item u
Unmark image
@item M
Mark all images
@item U
Unmark all
@item t
Toggle all marks
@end table

@subheading File Operations

@table @kbd
@item D
Delete image at point
@item C-d
Delete image and move to next
@item x
Delete all marked images
@item d
Jump to file in Dired
@end table

@subheading Other

@table @kbd
@item W
Open in external editor
@item ?
@itemx h
Show help
@end table

@node Image Display Buffer Keys
@section In Image Display Buffer

@table @kbd
@item C-d
Delete image and move to next
@end table

All standard @code{image-dired} keybindings (@kbd{n}, @kbd{p}, @kbd{m},
@kbd{u}, @kbd{U}, etc.) continue to work as expected.

@node Header Line
@chapter Header Line

The enhanced header line displays:

@itemize @bullet
@item
@strong{Mark indicator} --- A @samp{*} if the current image is marked
@item
@strong{Filename} --- Relative to source directory when subdirectories are inserted
@item
@strong{Directory} --- Location of the current image, abbreviated (e.g., @samp{~/Photos/}); falls back to the source directory
@item
@strong{Image count} --- Current position / total (e.g., @samp{23/156})
@item
@strong{Dimensions} --- Width x Height in pixels (e.g., @samp{1920x1080})
@item
@strong{File size} --- Human-readable size (e.g., @samp{2.4M})
@item
@strong{Sort indicator} --- Current sort field and direction (e.g., @samp{[name <]})
@item
@strong{Display quality} --- Current quality level (e.g., @samp{[fast]})
@item
@strong{Active filters} --- Description of any active filters
@item
@strong{Marked count} --- Number of marked images (e.g., @samp{[3 marked]})
@end itemize

@node Customization
@chapter Customization

All customization options are in the @code{dired-image-thumbnail} group.
Use @kbd{M-x customize-group @key{RET} dired-image-thumbnail @key{RET}}
to browse them interactively.

@menu
* Default Sort Settings::       Sorting defaults
* Display Options::             Wrap display mode
* Window Layout::               Split-screen layout presets
* Display Quality::             Speed vs fidelity trade-off
* Image Validation::            Corrupt file detection
* External Editor::             Open images externally
* Navigation Behavior::         Auto-display on navigate
* Auto-Accepting Actions::      Skip confirmation prompts
* Image Extensions::            Recognised file types
@end menu

@node Default Sort Settings
@section Default Sort Settings

@lisp
(setq dired-image-thumbnail-sort-by 'dired)       ; 'dired, 'name, 'date, 'size, or 'dimensions
(setq dired-image-thumbnail-sort-order 'ascending) ; 'ascending or 'descending
@end lisp

@node Display Options
@section Display Options

@lisp
(setq dired-image-thumbnail-wrap-display nil) ; Enable wrap display by default
@end lisp

@node Window Layout
@section Window Layout

Control the split-screen layout and thumbnail/image ratio:

@lisp
(setq dired-image-thumbnail-window-layout 'left-right) ; 'left-right, 'right-left, 'top-bottom, 'bottom-top, 'thumb-only, or nil
(setq dired-image-thumbnail-window-ratio 0.4)          ; Fraction of frame for thumbnails
@end lisp

Set to @code{nil} to disable automatic layout management and use your own
@code{display-buffer-alist} rules.

@node Display Quality
@section Display Quality

Control the speed/fidelity trade-off when navigating with @kbd{n}/@kbd{p}:

@lisp
(setq dired-image-thumbnail-display-quality 'fast) ; 'full, 'high, 'fast, 'faster, or 'draft
@end lisp

Lower quality levels use external tools (@code{djpeg}/@code{cjpeg} for
JPEGs, @code{magick} for others) to generate small preview files, so Emacs
decodes less data.  Press @kbd{Q} in the thumbnail buffer to cycle through
levels interactively.

@node Image Validation
@section Image Validation

Control which files are accepted as images:

@lisp
(setq dired-image-thumbnail-minimum-file-size 100) ; Minimum bytes (0 to disable)
(setq dired-image-thumbnail-validate-headers t)    ; Check magic bytes
@end lisp

When @code{dired-image-thumbnail-validate-headers} is non-nil, each
candidate file is opened briefly to verify that its first few bytes match a
known image format signature (JPEG, PNG, GIF, BMP, TIFF, WEBP, ICO,
HEIC/HEIF).  SVG files are accepted without a byte check since they are XML
text.

@node External Editor
@section External Editor

Set a specific program for @kbd{W} to open images with:

@lisp
(setq dired-image-thumbnail-external-editor "gimp") ; nil for system default
@end lisp

When @code{nil} (default), the system default application is used via
@code{xdg-open} on Linux, @code{open} on macOS, or @code{start} on
Windows.

@node Navigation Behavior
@section Navigation Behavior

Control whether navigating with @kbd{n}/@kbd{p} automatically displays
full-size images:

@lisp
(setq dired-image-thumbnail-auto-display-on-navigate t) ; Auto-display on n/p
@end lisp

When enabled (default), pressing @kbd{n} or @kbd{p} in the thumbnail
buffer automatically updates the image display buffer.  When disabled, you
must press @key{RET} or @kbd{C-@key{RET}} to view full-size images.

@node Auto-Accepting Actions
@section Auto-Accepting Actions

Control whether to skip confirmation prompts for file actions:

@lisp
(setq dired-image-thumbnail-auto-accept nil) ; Require confirmation (default)
@end lisp

When enabled, actions like deleting files (@kbd{D}, @kbd{C-d}, @kbd{x})
will proceed without asking for confirmation.

@node Image Extensions
@section Image Extensions

Add or modify recognized image file extensions:

@lisp
(setq dired-image-thumbnail-image-extensions
      '("jpg" "jpeg" "png" "gif" "bmp" "tiff" "tif" "webp" "svg" "ico" "heic" "heif"))
@end lisp

@node Example Configuration
@chapter Example Configuration

@lisp
(use-package dired-image-thumbnail
  :load-path "/path/to/dired-image-thumbnail/"
  :demand t
  :custom
  (dired-image-thumbnail-sort-by 'date)
  (dired-image-thumbnail-sort-order 'descending)
  (dired-image-thumbnail-wrap-display t)
  (dired-image-thumbnail-window-layout 'left-right)
  (dired-image-thumbnail-auto-display-on-navigate t)
  :bind
  (:map dired-mode-map
   ("C-t d" . (lambda () (interactive)
                (image-dired default-directory)
                (dired-image-thumbnail-refresh)))
   ("C-t m" . dired-image-thumbnail)
   ("C-t s" . dired-image-thumbnail-insert-image-subdirs)
   ("C-t z" . dired-image-thumbnail-insert-subdir-recursive)
   ("C-t k" . dired-image-thumbnail-kill-all-subdirs)))
@end lisp

