@node Transient Menu Support
@chapter Transient Menu Support

If @code{transient} is available, @code{dired-image-thumbnail} provides
interactive menus for sorting and filtering.  These can be accessed with:

@itemize @bullet
@item
@kbd{S} --- Sort menu (shows all sort options and current state)
@item
@kbd{\} --- Filter menu (shows all filter options and current filters)
@end itemize

To disable transient menus even when transient is installed, don't load
@file{dired-image-thumbnail-transient.el}.

@node Performance Notes
@chapter Performance Notes

@section Subdirectory Insertion

When working with large directory trees:

@itemize @bullet
@item
Use @code{dired-image-thumbnail-insert-image-subdirs} (@kbd{C-t s}) instead of @code{dired-image-thumbnail-insert-subdir-recursive} (@kbd{C-t z})
@item
The ``smart'' insertion only processes subdirectories containing images, which is much faster
@item
For very large collections, manually insert specific subdirectories with @kbd{i} as needed
@end itemize

@section Thumbnail Generation

First-time thumbnail generation can be slow for large images.  Thumbnails
are cached by @code{image-dired}, so subsequent viewing is fast.

@section Display Quality and Speed

Lower display quality levels (@code{faster}, @code{draft}) generate smaller
preview files using external tools, significantly reducing image decode
time.  For large photo collections, set the quality to @code{draft} for
the fastest navigation, then switch to @code{full} when you want to
examine an image in detail.

@node Troubleshooting
@chapter Troubleshooting

@section Images not appearing

@itemize @bullet
@item
Ensure @code{image-dired} is working: test with @kbd{C-t d} in a directory with images
@item
Check that file extensions are in @code{dired-image-thumbnail-image-extensions}
@item
Verify thumbnails are being created in @code{image-dired-dir}
@item
If images have correct extensions but are corrupt, try setting @code{dired-image-thumbnail-validate-headers} to @code{nil}
@end itemize

@section Subdirectories not showing images

@itemize @bullet
@item
Ensure subdirectories are actually inserted in the Dired buffer (use @kbd{i} or helper commands)
@item
Check that @code{dired-image-thumbnail-insert-image-subdirs} found subdirectories (watch for message)
@item
Verify files in subdirectories have recognized image extensions
@end itemize

@section Slow performance with many directories

@itemize @bullet
@item
Use @kbd{C-t s} (insert image subdirs only) instead of @kbd{C-t z} (insert all subdirs)
@item
Manually insert specific subdirectories with @kbd{i} as needed
@item
Consider filtering to reduce the number of visible thumbnails
@item
Lower the display quality with @kbd{Q} for faster navigation
@end itemize

@section Layout not splitting correctly

@itemize @bullet
@item
Ensure @code{dired-image-thumbnail-window-layout} is set to a layout symbol (default @code{left-right})
@item
Try a different layout preset: @code{top-bottom}, @code{right-left}, etc.
@item
Set to @code{nil} and manage windows manually if other packages conflict
@item
Manually delete other windows with @kbd{C-x 1} before launching
@end itemize

@section Auto-display not working

@itemize @bullet
@item
Ensure @code{dired-image-thumbnail-auto-display-on-navigate} is @code{t} (default)
@item
The feature requires the split-screen layout to be active
@item
Try pressing @key{RET} on a thumbnail to manually trigger display
@end itemize

@node Related Packages
@chapter Related Packages

